    <statement><p>Calculate the gradient of <m>h(x,y,z)=x^{3}y\frac{1}{z}</m></p>
<p><m>\nabla h=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;3x^{2}y\frac{1}{z},x^{3}\frac{1}{z},-x^{3}y\frac{1}{z^{2}}\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>h(x,y,z)=x^{3}y\frac{1}{z}</m>, obtaining
<me>\frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{x}}=3x^{2}y\frac{1}{z} \quad \frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{y}}=x^{3}\frac{1}{z} \quad \frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{z}}=-x^{3}y\frac{1}{z^{2}}</me>
The gradient vector is thus
<me>\nabla h=\left\lt \frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{x}},\frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{y}},\frac{\partial{h}}{\partial{z}}\right&gt;=
\left\lt 3x^{2}y\frac{1}{z}, x^{3}\frac{1}{z}, -x^{3}y\frac{1}{z^{2}} \right&gt;</me>






</solution>
